summary run apps inside lightweight isolated boxes (containers) that work anywhere
sub run start a container from an image
sub ps list running containers
sub pull download an image from Docker Hub
sub build build a new image from a Dockerfile
sub images list images you have downloaded
sub stop stop a running container
flag -i interactive: keep stdin open so you can type into the container
flag -t allocate a terminal inside the container (usually combined with -i as -it)
flag -d run in the background (detached) and print the container id
